    {
      "id": "QDa1JBy3ZmOUKA-5Me0oR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -66.9919919134129,
      "y": 1773.5190588489093,
      "width": 1113.13330078125,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 399822957,
      "version": 1831,
      "versionNonce": 989668589,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792512274402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n \n1.Data Model and API\n    a) Server holding vector of 64-bit float per key (64-bit integers; value width >= 1)\n    b) Client library must offer:\n        i) push\n        ii) pull\n        iii) wait\n        iv) register server-side rule update\n    c) Additional requirements\n        i) support explicit key lists(sparse) and contiguous ranges (dense)\n        ii) Server aggregates pushed values(sum) and applies a configurable update rule (default: SGD, w <- w - ng),\n            concurrent pushes to one key must not be lost or corrupted\n        iii) calls are async: push and pull return a handle immediately; wait blocks\n\n2. Ease of use\n    a) Design the API so that worker author can write a training loop in about 10 lines, \n        without caring where the key lives\n    b) Document the API\n    c) Give meaningful errors\n    d) Write a short quick-start example\n\n3. Local task and dependencies\n    a) task may depends on earlier handles, server must not run it until they complete\n\n4. Single-node tests\n    a) unit test that concurrently pushes aggregate correctly, that ranges and key lists agree and \n        that dependencies are honoured\n\n\n\n          ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n \n1.Data Model and API\n    a) Server holding vector of 64-bit float per key (64-bit integers; value width >= 1)\n    b) Client library must offer:\n        i) push\n        ii) pull\n        iii) wait\n        iv) register server-side rule update\n    c) Additional requirements\n        i) support explicit key lists(sparse) and contiguous ranges (dense)\n        ii) Server aggregates pushed values(sum) and applies a configurable update rule (default: SGD, w <- w - ng),\n            concurrent pushes to one key must not be lost or corrupted\n        iii) calls are async: push and pull return a handle immediately; wait blocks\n\n2. Ease of use\n    a) Design the API so that worker author can write a training loop in about 10 lines, \n        without caring where the key lives\n    b) Document the API\n    c) Give meaningful errors\n    d) Write a short quick-start example\n\n3. Local task and dependencies\n    a) task may depends on earlier handles, server must not run it until they complete\n\n4. Single-node tests\n    a) unit test that concurrently pushes aggregate correctly, that ranges and key lists agree and \n        that dependencies are honoured\n\n\n\n          ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
