      "text": "C. Distribution, vector clocks & relaxed consistency",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "C. Distribution, vector clocks & relaxed consistency",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "RPekcXkLSf2MLVssGn5KN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1278.5367867733607,
      "y": 1751.6703191551612,
      "width": 1315,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 925423171,
      "version": 3130,
      "versionNonce": 1781621133,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792512274402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n \n1. Partitioning\n    a) split the key space over S servers (consistent hashing, or range partitioning with a manager-held table)\n    b) Server manager\n        i) implement a server manager that assigns key ranges and publishes the ownership map.\n        ii) client cache the map and refresh it when told it is stale\n    c) vector clocks per range\n        i) server keeps vector clocks recording, per key range, the latest update received from each worker, msg carry the relevant clock\n        ii) start with 1 clock per server partition and split a clock when a range is partially updated\n    d) Consistency models, using task dependencies (A3) as the mechanism and vector clocks to detect satisfied dependencies, \n        as a selectable option, implement:\n        i) sequential\n        ii) eventual\n        iii) bounded delay\n    e) Evaluate\n        i) compare throughput and convergence for the 3 models for serveral Tau, with and without stragglers\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n \n1. Partitioning\n    a) split the key space over S servers (consistent hashing, or range partitioning with a manager-held table)\n    b) Server manager\n        i) implement a server manager that assigns key ranges and publishes the ownership map.\n        ii) client cache the map and refresh it when told it is stale\n    c) vector clocks per range\n        i) server keeps vector clocks recording, per key range, the latest update received from each worker, msg carry the relevant clock\n        ii) start with 1 clock per server partition and split a clock when a range is partially updated\n    d) Consistency models, using task dependencies (A3) as the mechanism and vector clocks to detect satisfied dependencies, \n        as a selectable option, implement:\n        i) sequential\n        ii) eventual\n        iii) bounded delay\n    e) Evaluate\n        i) compare throughput and convergence for the 3 models for serveral Tau, with and without stragglers\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
