    {
      "id": "S_DTbvZASaRiVNHR2SPMr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2963.8930950688937,
      "y": 1760.4461508820254,
      "width": 1355.1666259765625,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 762401613,
      "version": 4086,
      "versionNonce": 1589646285,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792512274402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n \n1. Pick at least 3 of the following, implement them and measure the effect on bytes sent and latency ( and on convergence where relevant)\n   Report the savings as :  Saving = 1 - (Boptimized - Bbaseline)\n    a) Key caching\n        i) if a worker and server repeatedly exchange the same key set, send a short signature instead of the whole list.\n    b) Value compression\n        i) e.g. snappy, zstd, or run-length enconding of sparse deltas\n    c) Batching\n        i) small request into fewer msg\n    d) Aggregation before replication (related to part F)\n        i) one replication msg per batch of worker pushers\n    e) Filter\n        i) send only values that changes by more than a threshold or use reduced- precision values\n    f) Request pipelining\n        i) over the async API\n        ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n \n1. Pick at least 3 of the following, implement them and measure the effect on bytes sent and latency ( and on convergence where relevant)\n   Report the savings as :  Saving = 1 - (Boptimized - Bbaseline)\n    a) Key caching\n        i) if a worker and server repeatedly exchange the same key set, send a short signature instead of the whole list.\n    b) Value compression\n        i) e.g. snappy, zstd, or run-length enconding of sparse deltas\n    c) Batching\n        i) small request into fewer msg\n    d) Aggregation before replication (related to part F)\n        i) one replication msg per batch of worker pushers\n    e) Filter\n        i) send only values that changes by more than a threshold or use reduced- precision values\n    f) Request pipelining\n        i) over the async API\n        ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
