    {
      "id": "tVZdJkqCqu6ZpI_Y2HlKG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2956.243743747651,
      "y": 2234.006230530944,
      "width": 1468.933349609375,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2057079725,
      "version": 5264,
      "versionNonce": 2082417389,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792512274402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Adding a server at runtime\n    a) Manager assigns the newcomer a range, either vacant or split from a heavily loaded server\n    b) The new server must fatch the range from the precious owners while the system keeps serving requests\n    c) Pushes that arrive during the transfer must not be lost, use a 2-phase transfer (bulk copy, then delta changes since copy began) or forwarding\n    d) Existing servers then relinquish the range and clients learn the new map\n2. Removing a server gracefully\n    a) hand its range to others without losing data\n3. Adding and removing workers\n    a) workers join or leave mid-training\n    b) vector clocks and consistency bookkeeping must tolerate a changing worker set\n4. Demonstrate\n    a) run a harness scenario that doubles the number of servers mid-run.\n    b) plot thorughput and latency over time with the transition marked\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Adding a server at runtime\n    a) Manager assigns the newcomer a range, either vacant or split from a heavily loaded server\n    b) The new server must fatch the range from the precious owners while the system keeps serving requests\n    c) Pushes that arrive during the transfer must not be lost, use a 2-phase transfer (bulk copy, then delta changes since copy began) or forwarding\n    d) Existing servers then relinquish the range and clients learn the new map\n2. Removing a server gracefully\n    a) hand its range to others without losing data\n3. Adding and removing workers\n    a) workers join or leave mid-training\n    b) vector clocks and consistency bookkeeping must tolerate a changing worker set\n4. Demonstrate\n    a) run a harness scenario that doubles the number of servers mid-run.\n    b) plot thorughput and latency over time with the transition marked\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
