    },
    {
      "id": "Wo6gdc9-af1WzsCBLrEnC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4564.771580110482,
      "y": 1734.4416274978084,
      "width": 1392.4666748046875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 260940109,
      "version": 5281,
      "versionNonce": 1312803949,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792512274402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n \n1. Failure Detection\n    a) Heartbeats with a configurable timeout\n2. Replication\n    a) Replicate each range on K >= 1 neighbours\n    b) Acknowledge a push only after it is replicated, \n        make replication frequency configurable ( per push vs after aggregating a batch)\n3. Server Failure and Recovery\n    a) when a server is killed, promote a replica, update the ownership map and retry/ redirect in-flight request without applying any push twice\n        (task ids and vector clock give idempotence) training must continue\n4. Worker failure\n    a) a crashed worker must not block sequential or bounded-delay consistency forever\n    b) design and implement a policy (for example exclude it after a timeout)\n5. Failure matrix\n    a) Using a harness, run and report at least:\n        i) kill 1 server mid-iteration\n        ii) kill a server during a range transfer\n        iii) kill a worker under bounded delay\n        iv) delay or drop messages",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n \n1. Failure Detection\n    a) Heartbeats with a configurable timeout\n2. Replication\n    a) Replicate each range on K >= 1 neighbours\n    b) Acknowledge a push only after it is replicated, \n        make replication frequency configurable ( per push vs after aggregating a batch)\n3. Server Failure and Recovery\n    a) when a server is killed, promote a replica, update the ownership map and retry/ redirect in-flight request without applying any push twice\n        (task ids and vector clock give idempotence) training must continue\n4. Worker failure\n    a) a crashed worker must not block sequential or bounded-delay consistency forever\n    b) design and implement a policy (for example exclude it after a timeout)\n5. Failure matrix\n    a) Using a harness, run and report at least:\n        i) kill 1 server mid-iteration\n        ii) kill a server during a range transfer\n        iii) kill a worker under bounded delay\n        iv) delay or drop messages",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
